# Root-level ignores. `proven/.gitignore` only covers paths under proven/, so
# anything sitting at the repository root needs to be named here as well.

# ── Credentials ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Loose credential notes. A Xero client id is not itself a secret, but a bare
# credential file at the repo root is how a client SECRET eventually ends up in
# git history. Keep it out of the index.
xero_client_id.txt
*_client_id.txt
*_secret*.txt
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Python ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
*.sqlite
*.db

# ── Scratch files from debugging ─────────────────────────────────────────────
_ptest.py
_ptest_out.txt
_f2.txt
_f5.txt

# ── Stale duplicate trees ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SFF/ is an accidental triple-nested copy of this repository (SFF/SFF/SFF/...),
# frozen at 16 Aug 2026 and ~2 days behind root. Nothing exists only in there.
# Committing it would double the repo and confuse the "no ported code" evidence
# that clause 12.1(o)(iii) requires.
SFF/
_snapshot-before-ui-merge-20260816-0553/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
.env
